{
  "rationale": "The plant automata model the robot's perception (obstacle sensors) and motion capabilities (discrete actions). The specification automata bind sensor outcomes to safe, progress-oriented actions, enforce conservative but non-repetitive recovery, and ensure full_rotate and move_backward are used only as last-resort or brief escape actions. The design prioritizes forward and exploratory motion, with rapid return to exploration after recovery, and strictly prevents unsafe or oscillatory behaviors.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for perception and motion: G1 models obstacle sensor outcomes as uncontrollable events; G2 models discrete motion commands as controllable events.",
    "Specification automata E1 binds perception to safe action selection, ensures conservative recovery, and enforces correct usage of move_backward and full_rotate. E2 prevents repeated rotation or recovery actions, and E3 ensures forward/random_walk actions are not repeated without sensor update."
  ],
